uguese)\",\"language_code\":\"pt-br\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/pt-br/library/bg/11/55/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Русский (Russian)\",\"language_code\":\"ru\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/ru/library/bg/11/55/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Slovenčina (Slovak)\",\"language_code\":\"sk\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/sk/library/bg/11/55/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Slovenščina (Slovenian)\",\"language_code\":\"sl\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/sl/library/bg/11/55/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Українська мова (Ukrainian)\",\"language_code\":\"uk\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/uk/library/bg/11/55/\"},{\"display_name\":\"isiZulu (Zulu)\",\"language_code\":\"zu\",\"enabled\":false,\"url_path\":\"/zu/\"}],\"breadcrumb\":[{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/\",\"title\":\"Library\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Eleven: The Universal Form\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/\",\"bb\":3048,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/54/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 54\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/12/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Twelve\",\"has_advanced_view\":true,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":3462,\"bb\":568333,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"मत्कर्मकृन्मत्परमो मद्भ‍क्त: सङ्गवर्जित: ।
निर्वैर: सर्वभूतेषु य: स मामेति पाण्डव ॥ ५५ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3463,\"bb\":3049,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3049/\",\"body_value\":\"mat-karma-kṛn mat-paramo
mad-bhaktaḥ saṅga-varjitaḥ
nirvairaḥ sarva-bhūteṣu
yaḥ sa mām eti pāṇḍava\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3464,\"bb\":3050,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3050/\",\"shadow_value\":\"mat-karma-kṛt – engaged in doing My work; mat-paramaḥ – considering Me the Supreme; mat-bhaktaḥ – engaged in My devotional service; saṅga-varjitaḥ – freed from the contamination of fruitive activities and mental speculation; nirvairaḥ – without an enemy; sarva-bhūteṣu – among all living entities; yaḥ – one who; saḥ – he; mām – unto Me; eti – comes; pāṇḍava – O son of Pāṇḍu.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"mat-karma-kṛt\",\"translation\":\"engaged in doing My work\"},{\"word\":\"mat-paramaḥ\",\"translation\":\"considering Me the Supreme\"},{\"word\":\"mat-bhaktaḥ\",\"translation\":\"engaged in My devotional service\"},{\"word\":\"saṅga-varjitaḥ\",\"translation\":\"freed from the contamination of fruitive activities and mental speculation\"},{\"word\":\"nirvairaḥ\",\"translation\":\"without an enemy\"},{\"word\":\"sarva-bhūteṣu\",\"translation\":\"among all living entities\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"},{\"word\":\"mām\",\"translation\":\"unto Me\"},{\"word\":\"eti\",\"translation\":\"comes\"},{\"word\":\"pāṇḍava\",\"translation\":\"O son of Pāṇḍu\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3465,\"bb\":3051,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3051/\",\"body_value\":\"My dear Arjuna, he who engages in My pure devotional service, free from the contaminations of fruitive activities and mental speculation, he who works for Me, who makes Me the supreme goal of his life, and who is friendly to every living being – he certainly comes to Me.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3466,\"bb\":3052,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3052/\",\"body_value\":\"Anyone who wants to approach the supreme of all the Personalities of Godhead, on the Kṛṣṇaloka planet in the spiritual sky, and be intimately connected with the Supreme Personality, Kṛṣṇa, must take this formula, as stated by the Supreme Himself. Therefore, this verse is considered to be the essence of Bhagavad-gītā. The Bhagavad-gītā is a book directed to the conditioned souls, who are engaged in the material world with the purpose of lording it over nature and who do not know of the real, spiritual life. The Bhagavad-gītā is meant to show how one can understand his spiritual existence and his eternal relationship with the supreme spiritual personality and to teach one how to go back home, back to Godhead. Now here is the verse which clearly explains the process by which one can attain success in his spiritual activity: devotional service.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3467,\"bb\":3053,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3053/\",\"body_value\":\"As far as work is concerned, one should transfer his energy entirely to Kṛṣṇa conscious activities. As stated in the Bhakti-rasāmṛta-sindhu (1.2.255),\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3468,\"bb\":3054,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3054/\",\"body_value\":\"anāsaktasya viṣayān
yathārham upayuñjataḥ
nirbandhaḥ kṛṣṇa-sambandhe
yuktaṁ vairāgyam ucyate\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3469,\"bb\":3055,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3055/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3470,\"bb\":3056,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3056/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3471,\"bb\":3057,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3057/\",\"body_value\":\"The term saṅga-varjitaḥ is very significant. One should disassociate himself from persons who are against Kṛṣṇa. Not only are the atheistic persons against Kṛṣṇa, but so also are those who are attracted to fruitive activities and mental speculation. Therefore the pure form of devotional service is described in Bhakti-rasāmṛta-sindhu (1.1.11) as follows:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":3472,\"bb\":3058,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3058/\",\"body_value\":\"anyābhilāṣitā-śūnyaṁ
jñāna-karmādy-anāvṛtam
ānukūlyena kṛṣṇānu-
śīlanaṁ bhaktir uttamā\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3473,\"bb\":3059,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3059/\",\"body_value\":\"$27\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3474,\"bb\":3060,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3060/\",\"body_value\":\"$28\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3475,\"bb\":3061,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3061/\",\"body_value\":\"In summary, the universal form of Kṛṣṇa, which is a temporary manifestation, and the form of time which devours everything, and even the form of Viṣṇu, four-handed, have all been exhibited by Kṛṣṇa. Thus Kṛṣṇa is the origin of all these manifestations. It is not that Kṛṣṇa is a manifestation of the original viśva-rūpa, or Viṣṇu. Kṛṣṇa is the origin of all forms. There are hundreds and thousands of Viṣṇus, but for a devotee no form of Kṛṣṇa is important but the original form, two-handed Śyāmasundara. In the Brahma-saṁhitā it is stated that those who are attached to the Śyāmasundara form of Kṛṣṇa in love and devotion can see Him always within the heart and cannot see anything else. One should understand, therefore, that the purport of this Eleventh Chapter is that the form of Kṛṣṇa is essential and supreme.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph_end\",\"id\":3476,\"bb\":3062,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/11/55/b3062/\",\"body_value\":\"Thus end the Bhaktivedanta Purports to the Eleventh Chapter of the Śrīmad Bhagavad-gītā in the matter of the Universal Form.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 11.55\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 11.55\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2d:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv